# test_runs.log

Purpose:
Record public test runs, self-test runs, score progression, and failure categories.

Judges should be able to see how the agent improved over time.

Format:

[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] TEST_RUN
Run by: agent/human
Command:
Suite: public/self-generated/manual smoke
Score/result:
Main failing categories:
Agent response/next step:

Examples:

[2026-05-21 20:52] TEST_RUN
Run by: agent
Command: python3 secret_spec/test_runner/run_tests.py --program "python3 solution.py" --suite public
Suite: public
Score/result: 31/250
Main failing categories: CLI output, valid basic cases, JSON schema
Agent response/next step: Implement required stdout JSON structure and correct exit codes.

[2026-05-21 22:06] TEST_RUN
Run by: agent
Command: python3 secret_spec/test_runner/run_tests.py --program "python3 solution.py" --suite public
Suite: public
Score/result: 143/250
Main failing categories: nested cases, multi-error recovery, boundary/stress
Agent response/next step: Focus on nested structures and exact invalid-output schema.

[2026-05-22 01:20] TEST_RUN
Run by: agent
Command: python3 tests/self_generated/test_exit_codes.py
Suite: self-generated
Score/result: 5/6 passed
Main failing categories: usage error stdout not empty
Agent response/next step: Patch CLI usage handler to print diagnostics only to stderr.

[2026-05-22 08:55] TEST_RUN
Run by: human
Command: python3 secret_spec/test_runner/run_tests.py --program "python3 solution.py" --suite public
Suite: public
Score/result: 226/250
Main failing categories: stress boundary and rare edge policy
Agent response/next step: Final run before submission. No manual code edits.
